    <h2>The Three Domains of CLIA</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card purple">
        <h3>Epistemic Domain</h3>
        <p>Truth verification layer. Validates all inputs through source checks, logic gap analysis, and deception detection. Confidence discipline enforced: ≤75% ceiling, 75–95% near‑absolute verification, 95% maximum.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card orange">
        <h3>Analytical Domain</h3>
        <p>Forecasting engine. Detects global inflection points via signal mapping, pressure analysis, and timing precision. Forecasts remain probabilistic, never declarative.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card teal">
        <h3>Operational Domain</h3>
        <p>Decision OS. Translates verified forecasts into adaptive action states across Shock, Trend, Narrative, Compression, and Transition regimes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Unified Flow -->
  <section id="flow">
